## 🚀 Free Hosting Guide (Complete Step-by-Step)

The SCL platform is composed of four main components. Here is how you can host each of them entirely for free:

```mermaid
graph TD
    User([User Browser]) -->|HTTPS| Frontend[Vercel: React SPA]
    Frontend -->|API / WebSockets| Backend[Railway: Spring Boot]
    Backend -->|JDBC SSL| DB[Supabase: PostgreSQL]
    Backend -->|REST| AIService[Render: FastAPI]
    AIService -->|HTTPS| LLM[Groq Cloud API]
```

### 1. Database: PostgreSQL (Supabase)
Since you are already using Supabase, you are already using their **Free Tier** (includes 500MB database storage, which is plenty for metadata).
- Ensure your database stays running.
- Ensure your table schemas are owned and initialized by Liquibase in the backend.

---

### 2. LLM: Replace Local Ollama with Groq (Cloud LLM)
Since running Ollama locally on a free host is not possible (requires high GPU/RAM), we will use **Groq** which is free and offers high-performance cloud LLMs (Llama 3).
1. Go to [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com/) and register for a free account.
2. Generate an **API Key**.
3. Your FastAPI AI service will automatically use Groq when `GROQ_API_KEY` is provided, bypassing Ollama completely!

---

### 3. AI Microservice: FastAPI (Render)
Render offers a free tier for web services (FastAPI/Python).

#### Step A: Push code to GitHub
Create a separate repository or select your main repository on GitHub.

#### Step B: Deploy to Render
1. Go to [Render.com](https://render.com) and log in using GitHub.
2. Click **New** -> **Web Service**.
3. Select your repository.
4. Set the following settings:
   - **Name:** `scl-ai-service`
   - **Language:** `Python`
   - **Build Command:** `pip install -r scl-ai-service/requirements.txt`
   - **Start Command:** `uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`
   - Make sure to specify the sub-folder if your repo is nested (you can use Render's **Root Directory** setting: `scl-ai-service`).
5. Under **Environment Variables**, add:
   - `GROQ_API_KEY` = `your_groq_api_key_here`
   - `GROQ_MODEL` = `llama-3.1-8b-instant`
   - `SUPABASE_URL` = `your_supabase_url_here`
   - `SUPABASE_KEY` = `your_supabase_anon_or_service_key`
6. Click **Deploy Web Service**. Render will assign a public HTTPS URL like `https://scl-ai-service.onrender.com`.

> [!NOTE]
> Free instances on Render spin down (sleep) after 15 minutes of inactivity. When a new request arrives, it might take ~50 seconds to boot up.

---

### 4. Backend: Spring Boot 3.3 (Railway or Render)
Since Spring Boot requires Java 21, **Railway** is the easiest free/low-cost container platform, or you can deploy on **Render** using Docker.

#### Option A: Railway (Highly Recommended)
Railway gives free trial credits ($5 value) every month, which is perfect for development:
1. Go to [Railway.app](https://railway.app) and sign up.
2. Click **New Project** -> **Deploy from GitHub repo**.
3. Select your repository. Under settings, select root directory as `scl-backend`.
4. Railway will auto-detect the Maven project and build it.
5. In the **Variables** tab, add your environment variables:
   - `DB_URL` = `jdbc:postgresql://db.phoxiknwaamugdhbacfv.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require`
   - `DB_USER` = `postgres`
   - `DB_PASSWORD` = `your_supabase_db_password`
   - `JWT_SECRET` = `your_long_base64_jwt_secret`
   - `AI_SERVICE_URL` = `https://scl-ai-service.onrender.com` (from your Render deployment)
   - `MAIL_USERNAME` = `your_email@gmail.com`
   - `MAIL_PASSWORD` = `your_app_password`
   - `SUPABASE_URL` = `your_supabase_url`
   - `SUPABASE_KEY` = `your_supabase_key`
6. Click **Deploy**. It will generate a backend API URL (e.g. `https://scl-backend.up.railway.app`).

---

### 5. Frontend: React App (Vercel)
Vercel is free forever for frontend React apps.

#### Step A: Configure Vite Configuration for Production
In production, your Vite proxy rules (`vite.config.js`) will not be running. The frontend must point directly to your live backend domain.
- We have already set up `lib/axios.js` to use `http://localhost:8080/api/v1` as baseline.
- **Before deploying**, open `scl-frontend/scl/src/lib/axios.js` and change `baseURL` to use your production Railway API URL:
  ```javascript
  const api = axios.create({
    baseURL: "https://scl-backend.up.railway.app/api/v1", // Your production backend URL
  });
  ```

#### Step B: Deploy to Vercel
1. Go to [Vercel.com](https://vercel.com) and sign up with GitHub.
2. Click **Add New** -> **Project**.
3. Select your repository.
4. Configure Project settings:
   - **Framework Preset:** `Vite`
   - **Root Directory:** `scl-frontend/scl`
   - **Build Command:** `npm run build`
   - **Output Directory:** `dist`
5. Click **Deploy**. Vercel will build your app and deploy it on a fast, global CDN for free! (e.g. `https://scl-library.vercel.app`).
